#### LOD and Culling

Implement LOD and culling to optimize rendering:

```cpp
void UpdateVehicleRendering(AActor* Vehicle, float DistanceToCamera) {
    if (DistanceToCamera > 1000.0f) {
        Vehicle->SetActorHiddenInGame(true);
    } else {
        Vehicle->SetActorHiddenInGame(false);
        if (DistanceToCamera > 500.0f) {
            Vehicle->SetLODLevel(1);
        } else {
            Vehicle->SetLODLevel(0);
        }
    }
}
```

#### Fixed Timestep for Physics

Use a fixed timestep for physics updates:

```cpp
void UpdatePhysics(float DeltaTime) {
    static float Accumulator = 0.0f;
    const float FixedDeltaTime = 0.0166667f; // Approximately 60 fps

    Accumulator += DeltaTime;

    while (Accumulator >= FixedDeltaTime) {
        // Perform physics update
        Accumulator -= FixedDeltaTime;
    }
}
```

#### Parallel Processing

Use Unreal Engine's task graph for parallel processing:

```cpp
void ProcessVehiclesParallel(TArray<AActor*>& Vehicles) {
    FGraphEventArray Tasks;
    for (AActor* Vehicle : Vehicles) {
        FAsyncTaskPtr Task(new FAsyncTask([Vehicle] {
            // Perform vehicle processing in parallel
        }));
        Task->StartBackgroundTask();
        Tasks.Add(Task);
    }

    for (FGraphEventPtr& Task : Tasks) {
        Task->WaitUntilFinished();
    }
}
```

